        timingType: "Chain (The 3.6 FSI utilizes the VR6 architecture with a highly complex timing chain system located at the rear of the engine, right up against the firewall. Over time, the chains are prone to stretching and the plastic chain guides become brittle and break. Because of its rearward placement, replacing the timing chain components is an incredibly labor-intensive 'engine-out' or 'transmission-out' service. It is vital to monitor chain phase adaptation via VCDS and listen for distinct rattling noises on cold starts to prevent catastrophic failure).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI. Fuel is injected directly into the combustion chamber at high pressures. Because no fuel washes over the back of the intake valves, this engine suffers from severe carbon buildup. This carbon choking restricts airflow, causing misfires, rough idling, and significant power loss, necessitating physical walnut blasting of the intake ports every 100,000 km).", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The cast-iron VR6 block itself is an incredibly durable, battle-proven design derived from VW's legendary VR6 lineage. The mechanical internals will easily last beyond 300,000 km. However, the vehicle's functional lifespan is often limited by the immense labor costs associated with rear timing chain replacement, catastrophic PCV valve failures blowing rear main seals, and general cooling system degradation).", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (The 3.6 FSI relies entirely on displacement and its narrow 10.6-degree VR6 cylinder angle to produce power. It features a dual-branch intake manifold with variable runner lengths to optimize low-end torque and high-end horsepower, delivering a very linear, smooth powerband with a distinct, legendary VR6 exhaust note).", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic MED 9.1 (A highly capable engine control unit managing the high-pressure fueling, continuous variable valve timing, and variable intake manifold flaps. As a naturally aspirated engine, software tuning yields very minimal horsepower gains, usually just optimizing throttle response).", euroStandard: "Euro 4", maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The VR6 rotating assembly is phenomenally strong. While naturally aspirated tuning maxes out around 300 hp, the stock internals can easily handle bolt-on supercharger kits running moderate boost, making it a highly robust foundation if forced induction is applied).",
