        commonIssues: [ "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The long, rear-mounted timing chains stretch over time, and the hydraulic tensioners lose pressure. Causes extreme cold-start rattling and eventual timing jump.", "PCV Valve Diaphragm Rupture: The Positive Crankcase Ventilation valve membrane tears, causing massive internal vacuum leaks, whistling noises, a rough idle, and severe oil consumption.", "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: The pure FSI direct injection system allows thick, hardened carbon deposits to form on the intake valves, choking the engine of air and causing cold misfires.", "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: While utilizing a more robust roller follower than the 2.0T, the HPFP and its cam lobe can still suffer wear if oil changes are neglected.", "Ignition Coil Pack Failure: The coils are located deep in the narrow VR6 cylinder head and degrade rapidly due to severe heat cycling, leading to ignition misfires under load.", "Variable Intake Manifold Flap Seizure: The plastic flaps inside the intake manifold can bind with carbon or wear out, throwing CEL codes and restricting torque." ],
        vulnerabilities: [ "Catastrophic Valvetrain Destruction - Ignoring a stretched timing chain or failing tensioner will inevitably cause the chain to jump teeth, bending the valves and destroying the cylinder head.", "Rear Main Seal Blowout - If the PCV valve fails and pressurizes the crankcase, the weakest point is the rear main seal. Replacing it requires dropping the transmission.", "Valve Seat Pitting - Severe, unaddressed carbon buildup on the intake valves can eventually cause the valves to improperly seat, leading to permanent pitting and loss of compression.", "Coolant Pipe Cracking - The plastic coolant distribution pipes attached to the block become incredibly brittle over a decade of heat cycling and will shatter without warning.", "Catalytic Converter Failure - Chronic misfires from bad coils or heavy carbon buildup will dump unburnt fuel into the exhaust, melting the expensive catalytic converters.", "09D Valve Body Failure - Neglecting the Aisin automatic transmission fluid leads to severe wear in the valve body, causing harsh, clunky shifts from 1st to 2nd gear." ],
